  "notes": "A stock Skeleton CSS boilerplate look: everything is monochrome #222 on white, with Raleway, 4px-radius buttons outlined in 1px #bbb, and hairline <hr> separators between rows. The only color comes from the podcast cover art (bold flat illustrated covers) and the green played-checkmark. Episode actions are small square outlined icon buttons (Font Awesome solid), and the set changes with download state: 'download to server' (cloud) vs 'download file' plus 'delete'. The H1 doubles as the live result count. Every filter, sort and paging setting is written to the URL query string. Filtering applies immediately without an apply button. The Podcasts and Tags controls are searchable multiselects that show removable tokens once something is selected (seen live; nothing is selected in the capture)."
